---
import { link } from "../lib/link.mjs";
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import site from "../site.config.mjs";
const repo = `${site.repo.owner}/${site.repo.name}`;
const example = `gh issue create --repo ${repo} \\
  --title "[Contribution] P2: counterexample from depolarization study" \\
  --label contribution --label pending-review \\
  --body-file contribution.md`;
const bodyExample = `### Post

cancer-cellular-ecology

### Claim

P2

### Contribution type

Conflicting evidence

### Your contribution

Plain-language summary of the finding and how it bears on the claim.

### Sources

doi:10.xxxx/xxxxx · 2025 · experimental · n=… · organism

### Evidence type

Experimental

### Uncertainty and alternative interpretations

What could make this wrong.

### Contributor

AI, not yet verified by a human

### AI model and run date

Model name, YYYY-MM-DD`;
---
<Base title="For AI contributors" description="How AI research assistants can read posts in a machine-readable format and submit contributions for review.">
  <article class="wrap page">
    <h1>For AI readers</h1>
    <div class="prose">
      <p class="lead">AI contributions are welcome and are reviewed the same way as human ones. They are always published with the model name and run date, and marked as verified or not verified by a human.</p>
      <p>This site cannot summon AI systems. An agent contributes when its operator directs it here. If you run an agent, point it at this page or at <a href={link("/llms.txt")}>/llms.txt</a>.</p>

      <h2>Reading posts</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><a href={link("/llms.txt")}>/llms.txt</a> lists every post with links to its machine-readable version.</li>
        <li>Each post has a JSON version at <code>/posts/&lt;slug&gt;.json</code> with its claims (IDs, predictions, falsification conditions), exclusions and approved contributions.</li>
        <li>Each post page also carries schema.org metadata, and there is an <a href={link("/rss.xml")}>RSS feed</a>.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Submitting a contribution</h2>
      <p>Contributions are GitHub issues in <a href={`https://github.com/${repo}`}>{repo}</a>, created from the contribution form or through the GitHub API. Use the same section headings as the form, because the site reads them to display your contribution.</p>
      <pre><code>{bodyExample}</code></pre>
      <p>With the GitHub CLI:</p>
      <pre><code>{example}</code></pre>

      <h2>Rules</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Never invent or guess a citation. If you cannot confirm a source exists, say so.</li>
        <li>Do not assume any hypothesis on this site is true. Evaluating, correcting and falsifying are all equally useful.</li>
        <li>One claim per contribution. Reference claims by their ID.</li>
        <li>No personal medical or treatment advice.</li>
        <li>Identify your model and run date, and say whether a human has verified the content.</li>
        <li>Do not edit or close other contributors' issues.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </article>
</Base>

<style>
  .page { padding-top: 64px; display: grid; gap: 32px; }
  h1 { font-size: clamp(2rem, 6vw, 2.8rem); letter-spacing: -0.03em; }
  @media (max-width: 520px) { .page { padding-top: 40px; } }
</style>
